1. Rights holder
   All rights in this software — source code, design, stylesheets, scripts,
   templates, documentation, screenshots, and the "NEOcms" logos and name —
   belong exclusively to Erich Nigg (NEO Digital), the "rights holder".

2. Use by the rights holder only
   The software may be used by the rights holder only. Nobody else is granted
   any right to the software, in whole or in part.

3. In particular, it is expressly not permitted to
   a) install or use the software — including for one's own websites, for
      clients or for testing;
   b) copy, distribute, publish or make it available to others;
   c) adapt, modify or translate it, or take any part of it (code, design,
      logos) into other software or designs;
   d) sell, rent or license it, or present it as one's own work — including
      in modified form or under another name.

4. Publicly visible does not mean free to use
   The source code being visible (for example in a public repository) grants
   no rights of use. Where a platform's terms of service (e.g. GitHub)
   necessarily allow other users to view the source code on that platform or
   to create a copy ("fork") there, that exact scope applies and nothing
   more; any further use is prohibited.

5. Installations by the rights holder
   When the rights holder installs the software on a website, this is use by
   the rights holder. The operator of that website acquires no rights to the
   software. The operator may only let it run in that installation set up by
   the rights holder, for as long as the rights holder allows — not copy,
   adapt, transfer it to other websites or pass it on. The rights holder may
   remove the software at any time.

6. Exceptions
   Any use beyond this licence requires the rights holder's prior written
   consent.

7. Infringements
   Any use not permitted infringes the rights holder's copyright and trademark
   rights and may give rise to claims for injunction, removal and damages.

8. Third-party components
   Contao itself is licensed under LGPL-3.0-or-later; this package extends
   Contao and contains no Contao source code. Bundled third-party components
   (icons, fonts) are licensed under their own terms — see THIRD-PARTY.md.
   This licence neither restricts nor extends those rights.

9. Warranty and liability
   The software is provided without warranty. Liability exists only where
   mandatory by law.

10. Governing law and venue
    Austrian law applies, excluding its conflict-of-law rules. The place of
    jurisdiction is the competent court for the rights holder's seat.
